{"ok": true, "result": [["BASE", "This notebook evaluates a zero-shot paraphrase detection workflow on the GLUE MRPC validation set using the typeform/distilbert-base-uncased-mnli natural language inference model. For each sentence pair, it runs inference in both directions (sentence1→sentence2 and sentence2→sentence1), computes an entailment-versus-contradiction margin for each direction, averages the two margins, and predicts paraphrase only when neither direction is classified as contradiction and the average margin is positive. The notebook stores per-example predictions, directional margins, and gate decisions in TableVault, computes accuracy, F1, and a classification report against the MRPC labels, logs error analysis examples, and saves dataset-, prediction-, summary-, and notebook-level metadata and embeddings for later retrieval and documentation.", "consensus_then_avg_margin_mrpc", "process_list"], ["BASE", "This notebook evaluates a simple paraphrase detection workflow on the GLUE MRPC validation set using DistilBERT sentence representations and cosine similarity. It loads sentence pairs and labels from TableVault, encodes each sentence with distilbert-base-uncased, uses the first-token ([CLS]-style) hidden state as a normalized embedding, computes cosine similarity between the two sentence embeddings, and applies a fixed threshold of 0.85 to predict whether the pair is a paraphrase. The notebook then measures performance with accuracy, F1, and a classification report, prints example predictions and errors for inspection, and stores per-example scores, summary metrics, and semantic descriptions back into TableVault for experiment tracking and retrieval.", "distilbert_cls_cosine_mrpc", "process_list"], ["BASE", "This notebook evaluates a simple semantic-similarity baseline for paraphrase detection on the GLUE MRPC validation set. It uses distilbert-base-uncased to encode each sentence, averages the last four hidden layers, applies mean pooling over tokens, and L2-normalizes the resulting sentence embeddings. For each sentence pair, it computes cosine similarity between the two embeddings and converts similarity scores into binary paraphrase predictions using a fixed threshold of 0.85. The workflow loads MRPC examples from TableVault, generates pairwise predictions and similarity scores, computes evaluation metrics including accuracy, F1, and a classification report, inspects example predictions and errors, and stores both per-example outputs and summary results back into TableVault with descriptive metadata.", "distilbert_last4_mean_cosine_mrpc", "process_list"], ["BASE", "This notebook evaluates a simple paraphrase detection pipeline on the GLUE MRPC validation set using DistilBERT sentence embeddings. It loads sentence pairs and labels from TableVault, encodes each sentence with distilbert-base-uncased, applies masked max pooling over token embeddings, L2-normalizes the pooled vectors, and computes cosine similarity between the two sentence embeddings. A fixed cosine threshold is used to convert similarity scores into binary paraphrase predictions, and the notebook reports accuracy, F1, a full classification report, and example errors. It also records per-example predictions, summary metrics, and workflow metadata back into TableVault, with OpenAI-generated description embeddings for searchable experiment documentation.", "distilbert_max_pool_cosine_mrpc", "process_list"], ["BASE", "This notebook runs a simple unsupervised paraphrase detection experiment on the GLUE MRPC validation set using distilbert-base-uncased sentence embeddings. It loads sentence pairs and labels from TableVault, encodes each sentence with DistilBERT, applies attention-mask mean pooling and L2 normalization, computes cosine similarity between the two sentence embeddings, and converts similarity scores into binary paraphrase predictions using the median similarity as the decision threshold. It then evaluates performance with accuracy, F1, and a classification report, inspects sample predictions and errors, and stores per-example predictions, cosine scores, summary metrics, and notebook-level metadata/descriptions in TableVault with OpenAI-generated description embeddings for documentation and retrieval.", "distilbert_mean_cosine_median_threshold_mrpc", "process_list"], ["BASE", "This notebook evaluates a simple paraphrase detection baseline on the GLUE MRPC validation set using DistilBERT sentence embeddings. It loads the distilbert-base-uncased model, encodes each sentence in a pair, mean-pools token embeddings while excluding special tokens such as [CLS] and [SEP], L2-normalizes the pooled vectors, and computes cosine similarity between the two sentence embeddings. A fixed similarity threshold of 0.85 is used to predict whether each pair is a paraphrase. The notebook then measures accuracy, F1, and a full classification report, inspects example predictions and errors, and stores per-example predictions, cosine scores, summary metrics, and notebook/process metadata in TableVault with embedding-based descriptions for later retrieval and documentation.", "distilbert_no_special_tokens_mean_cosine_mrpc", "process_list"], ["BASE", "This notebook evaluates a zero-shot paraphrase detection workflow on the GLUE MRPC validation set using an NLI model. It loads sentence pairs and labels from TableVault, applies the typeform/distilbert-base-uncased-mnli sequence classification model, and treats paraphrase detection as entailment scoring: for each pair, it computes the log-probability difference between entailment and contradiction for both sentence orders (sentence1→sentence2 and sentence2→sentence1), averages the two directional scores, and predicts paraphrase when the averaged score is positive. The notebook stores per-example predictions and directional entailment log-odds in TableVault, computes evaluation metrics including accuracy, F1, and a classification report, inspects sample predictions and errors, and saves both dataset-level summaries and notebook-level metadata/descriptions with OpenAI embeddings for documentation and retrieval.", "entailment_logprob_odds_mrpc", "process_list"], ["BASE", "This notebook evaluates google/flan-t5-small on the GLUE MRPC validation set for binary paraphrase detection. It loads sentence pairs and labels from TableVault, converts each pair into a natural-language prompt asking whether the two sentences have the same meaning, and runs FLAN-T5 as a seq2seq model on MPS or CPU. Using the decoder prefix Answer:, it compares the next-token logits for yes and no to make a classification without full text generation. The workflow saves per-example predictions and yes/no logits to TableVault, computes accuracy, F1, and a classification report, reviews sample predictions and errors, and stores both dataset-level outputs and experiment summary metadata/descriptions back into TableVault for tracking and retrieval.", "flan_t5_answer_prefix_yes_no_mrpc", "process_list"], ["BASE", "This notebook runs a zero-shot paraphrase detection experiment on the GLUE MRPC validation set using google/flan-t5-small. It frames each sentence pair as an instruction prompt asking whether the two sentences are paraphrases and scores the first decoder-step logits for the single-token answers yes and no. To reduce prompt bias, it applies contextual calibration by subtracting baseline yes/no logits computed from a null prompt with placeholder inputs (“N/A”, “N/A”), then predicts the label from the higher calibrated logit. The workflow loads MRPC examples from TableVault, generates batch predictions, stores raw and calibrated logits plus final predictions back into TableVault, computes evaluation metrics including accuracy, F1, and a classification report, inspects sample predictions and errors, and saves summary records and semantic descriptions for the prediction outputs, summary table, and overall notebook process.", "flan_t5_contextual_calibrated_yes_no_mrpc", "process_list"], ["BASE", "This notebook runs a prompt-based paraphrase detection experiment on the GLUE MRPC validation set using google/flan-t5-small. For each sentence pair, it builds an instruction prompt asking whether the two sentences are paraphrases and scores the full decoder log probability of the candidate answers “yes” and “no” (including EOS). The predicted label is chosen by comparing these two sequence log probabilities.

The workflow loads MRPC validation data from TableVault, tokenizes prompts, performs batched inference with FLAN-T5, records per-example predictions and yes/no scores, and evaluates performance with accuracy, F1, and a classification report. It also prints sample predictions and error cases for qualitative inspection.

Results are written back to TableVault as a scored prediction record list and a summary record list, with dataset lineage links and embedding-based descriptions/metadata for both the outputs and the overall notebook process.", "flan_t5_full_answer_logprob_mrpc", "process_list"]]}

